                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not your typical HOG. Great mix of adventure+point and click. \nGameplay Video:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Ga-ECY-Pzo\nPlaying as Maya Anderson, you travel to a mental institution in some attempt to help patients who have all recently gone 'insane'. That's where the fun begins. Stepping inside each patients subconscious by using your hypnosis powers will take you to a crazy world filled with objects related to thoughts of that person. \n\nOne of the first things you will notice inside these worlds are 'phobias'. Running into these enemies loads a battle scene where you must work cells along pathways to take majority control of the 'nodes', interesting blend and adds almost rpg-like elements. Further along you uncover missing pieces of the memory that will present you with 'puzzles', much more adventure-like in nature, generally involving simple combinations of items. Completing these tasks is the primary form of game progression.\n\nThe lovely artstyle and themes of each world alone make Hypnosis standout, while making you want to continue playing. Couple that with a well read fully voiced story and decent price, we have a winner. Cheers. :)",
